abstract: >
  First comprehensive school-exposure PM2.5 assessment for Central Asia, 
  analyzing 8,301 hourly measurements from Tashkent, Uzbekistan (January 
  2022 - June 2023). Study quantifies PM2.5 health impacts on 420,000 
  school-age children and provides evidence base for World Bank-UNEP 
  High-Level Policy Dialogue on Air Quality Management in Central Asia.
  
  Dataset includes: Raw hourly PM2.5 measurements from U.S. Embassy 
  Tashkent (OpenAQ Station 8881, Federal Equivalent Method monitor), 
  complete analysis scripts, statistical outputs, and reproducibility 
  materials.

